course: dictionary
lesson: 4000
title: Gangster: a criminal, or a tough guy?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gangster is a member of a gang of violent criminals who break the law to get money or power. «The gangsters robbed the bank and ran off with the money.» The clues are robbed, bank and ran off. Those are criminal actions, so a gangster is a criminal.
explain: Some young people also use «gangster» as slang for someone who acts tough or cool. «Jay wore his shades and said, "I'm such a gangster."» Jay is not a criminal here. The clue is that he is showing off how cool he is. Always ask: does the sentence fit a crime, or someone acting cool?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The gangsters threatened the shopkeeper» makes sense with the criminal meaning, but not with the cool meaning. Real gangs are dangerous, so if you ever see one, keep away and tell a trusted adult.
fact: A gangster is a member of a gang of violent criminals.
fact: Gangsters break the law to get money or power.
fact: In films and stories, gangsters often rob banks, carry weapons and threaten people.
fact: «Gangster» can also be slang for someone who acts tough or cool.
fact: Phrases to know: a gangster film, a gang of gangsters, gangster rap.
exercise: «The gangsters robbed the bank and ran off with the money.» What is a gangster? | A kind shopkeeper | A police officer who catches thieves | *A member of a gang of violent criminals who break the law | A bank worker who counts the money
exercise: Maya says her big brother is a gangster because he wears a cool hat and walks slowly. What does gangster mean here? | *Someone who acts tough or cool | A tall building | A kind neighbour | A violent criminal
exercise: In a gangster film, what do the gangsters usually do? | *Rob banks and threaten people | Bake cakes for the school fair | Plant trees in the park | Read stories to young children
test: Which best describes a gangster? | A cool trainer brand | A friendly neighbour who helps everyone | A person who sells ice cream | *A criminal who is part of a violent gang
test: Jay says, «He is such a gangster in those shades!» What does Jay probably mean? | *He is trying to look tough or cool | He is a police officer | He has robbed a bank | He is the leader of a prison
exam: If you ever see a real gang, what should you do? | Join them to make friends | *Keep away and tell a trusted adult | Film them on your phone | Go and ask them for money
